hits.text:
this is pure f*cking gold - Claude + Obsidian is my most-used setup, and here's how to get it in 3 steps

> Claude reads and writes directly into your vault - searches notes, creates files, drops content under specific headings, summarizes meetings into new notes

> if you run Obsidian as your second brain, this turns Claude into the thinking layer sitting on top of it

the setup, 3 steps:

1. install the "Local REST API" plugin in Obsidian, enable it, copy the API key

2. open your Claude Desktop config:

- Mac: ~/Library/Application Support/Claude/claude_desktop_config.json
- Windows: %APPDATA%/Claude/claude_desktop_config.json

3. paste this in:

{
  "mcpServers": {
    "mcp-obsidian": {
      "command": "uvx",
      "args": ["mcp-obsidian"],
      "env": {
        "OBSIDIAN_API_KEY": "your_key_here",
        "OBSIDIAN_HOST": "127.0.0.1",
        "OBSIDIAN_PORT": "27124"
      }
    }
  }
}

> restart Claude. done

now you can say "summarize my last meeting note and save it as a new file" and it just does it 👇

